{#- Speaker-authored bytes reach this block, so free text is fenced the way the
    baseline accusation_round.j2 / vote_ballot.j2 fence theirs: the whole
    transcript sits inside <transcript> delimiters and each spoken line is
    quoted with every line boundary flattened, so no speaker can start a line
    at column 0 and open a section this template's own structure owns (the
    "## Account comparisons" heading below). The structured rows carry speaker
    free text too (an accusation's or a corroboration's reason), and
    model_dump_json escapes only the boundaries below \x1f -- NEL (U+0085),
    LINE SEPARATOR (U+2028) and PARAGRAPH SEPARATOR (U+2029) pass through it
    intact -- so each serialized row is flattened by the same filter. The ids
    inside those rows are separately checked against the roster, room and task
    ids by meetings.public_accounts.validate_public_accounts before the turn
    records. -#}
## What players said
<transcript>
{% for turn in transcript.turns %}
[{{ turn.turn_id }}] {{ turn.speaker }} said: "{{ turn.free_text | flatten_lines | replace('"', "'") }}"
{% for obs in turn.observations %}
- [turn:{{ turn.turn_id }}:{% if obs.type == "whereabouts" %}whereabouts{% else %}obs{% endif %}:{{ loop.index0 }}] {{ turn.speaker }} stated {{ obs.model_dump_json() | flatten_lines }}
{% endfor %}
{% for claim in turn.claims %}
- [turn:{{ turn.turn_id }}:claim:{{ loop.index0 }}] {{ turn.speaker }} stated {{ claim.model_dump_json() | flatten_lines }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
</transcript>
## Account comparisons
{% for flag in account_flags %}
- {{ flag.description }}
{% else %}
No account conflict was identified. That does not establish anyone's innocence.
{% endfor %}
